"""
Device Bound Session Credentials for the sessions of an OpenID provider (Wolly.Op), after the protocol of Wolly.Dbsc.

offer gives the value of Secure-Session-Registration for a live session
that holds no binding yet.  register takes the proof the browser posts,
keeps its key under the owner Wolly.OpBase.bindingOwner names, and gives
the session cookie a new value that lives Wolly.Dbsc.boundSeconds.
refresh gives a new value for each proof over a fresh challenge; the value
before opens nothing from then on, and Wolly.OpBase.cookieSession counts
a bound session only while its last refresh is no older than
Wolly.Dbsc.boundSeconds.  A session that ended, ran past its limits, or
whose account is locked or gone ends its binding at the next refresh.

The form tokens of Wolly.Op.csrfToken hang on the cookie value, so a form
shown before a refresh is refused once after it.

Every registration and refresh with a proof is a line of the audit log:
dbsc-register and dbsc-refresh, with the subject, the session and the
outcome.
"""
import Standard.String (
    String,
    length
);
import Standard.Database (
    Database,
    Writing,
    DbError
);
import Standard.FcgiServer (
    Request
);
import Standard.Log (
    Log
);
import Wolly.OpBase (
    OpSettings
);
import Wolly.Op (
    Handover
);

module Wolly.OpDbsc is
    """
    The value of Secure-Session-Registration for the session of the cookie
    of request at now, with a new challenge and path: Right None when the
    browser holds no live session, the session is bound already, or path
    is no endpoint path of Wolly.Dbsc.
    No contract on the result: it is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [Q: Region, R: Region, S: Region, P: Region]
    function offer(request: &[Request, Q], db: &![Database[Writing], R], settings: &[OpSettings, S], path: Span[Nat8, P],
        now: Int64): Either[DbError, Option[String]]
        requires now > 0;

    """
    The value of Secure-Session-Registration for the session that step
    gives the browser, with a new challenge and path: the session of the
    session cookie among its cookies, when it lives and holds no binding.
    Right None otherwise.  For the answer of a login, whose request
    carries no session cookie yet.
    No contract on the result: it is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region, S: Region, H: Region, P: Region]
    function offerAfter(db: &![Database[Writing], R], settings: &[OpSettings, S], step: &[Handover, H], path: Span[Nat8, P],
        now: Int64): Either[DbError, Option[String]]
        requires now > 0;

    """
    The registration of the proof of request at now for the live session
    of its cookie, which holds no binding yet: 200 with the session
    instructions (refresh at refresh_path) and the cookie with its new
    value; 401 without such a session, 400 for a proof that does not hold,
    500 when the work could not be done.  ip goes to the audit line.
    """
    generic [Q: Region, R: Region, S: Region, L: Region, P: Region, A: Region]
    function register(request: &[Request, Q], db: &![Database[Writing], R], settings: &[OpSettings, S], log: &![Log, L],
        refresh_path: Span[Nat8, P], ip: Span[Nat8, A], now: Int64): String
        requires now > 0
        ensures length(&result) > 0;

    """
    The refresh of the binding of Sec-Secure-Session-Id in request at now:
    403 with a new Secure-Session-Challenge without a proof or with one of
    a challenge that is not open; 200 with the instructions and a new
    cookie value for a proof that holds while the session lives and its
    account is active; 401 otherwise, which ends the session in the
    browser; 400 without an id.  ip goes to the audit line.
    """
    generic [Q: Region, R: Region, S: Region, L: Region, P: Region, A: Region]
    function refresh(request: &[Request, Q], db: &![Database[Writing], R], settings: &[OpSettings, S], log: &![Log, L],
        refresh_path: Span[Nat8, P], ip: Span[Nat8, A], now: Int64): String
        requires now > 0
        ensures length(&result) > 0;
end module.
